Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:32:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] TEACH-KB-AUDIT: the Teach keypad ranges measured on this
 HT9050 (read only, no code change) -- golden's ranges would change 11 real
 teach positions

Package 119 warns that the web Teach page has almost no keypad range (GitLab INBOX 140). Before adding golden's ranges here, measured what they
would do: every golden uteach.dfm TEdit OnClick (523 edits, 40 handlers, enumerated), the range golden picks with this machine's branch
values (MachineTypeChoice = Type_HT9046_LS via 9050GPIB, CC_PTI, AUTO_EMPTY_COLOR 0, ...; Mot_Table soft limits), against runcfg teach.ini.

11 positions in use fall outside the 9046LS branch (LoaderY, InSht1Y, OutSht1Y, Fix1X-3X, Auto1Y-3Y, OutPickX/Y); 10 of them sit inside golden's
HT9045 branch. Golden's keypad clamps silently on OK and on Cancel (myQwertyKeyBoard.cpp:285-291, :364), so golden's ranges as-is would
turn Auto1 Y -55618 into -60000 at one tap. Also 30 zero-valued keys out of range, 63 edits whose axis is not in Mot_Table.
docs/TEACH_KB_RANGE_HT9050_20261002.md has every row and the options for EastSun; WORKLOG item 70 and section 4.

